From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 00:58:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] dovi_ccm: a base layer in HLG, composed as one in SMPTE ST 2084
 where its RPU declares its picture so

ETSI GS CCM 001 V1.1.1, clause 5.2.2 a), admits a base layer in SMPTE ST
2084 or in Recommendation ITU-R BT.1886. Dolby Vision profile 8.4 has one
in HLG (base layer signal compatibility 4: iPhone recordings among
others), which the clause does not name. The composer of libplacebo-9930
composed such a picture as if its base layer were in PQ, and so did
libplacebo's own reshaping, with nothing to say that this is what the
picture means.

What the picture means is in its RPU. The reshaping of the RPU takes the
base layer to the HDR picture that the RPU's display management metadata
describe, and those say its transfer: signal_eotf with three parameters,
and signal_bit_depth. CCM 001 sends a picture in SMPTE ST 2084 with
0xFFFF and three parameters 0 in those places (table 3, the values of
those bytes), and the output of its composer with signal_bit_depth =
hdr_bit_depth (clause 6.2.2). Read with FFmpeg's own RPU parser, the RPU
of Dolby's profile 8.4 sample and the static profile 8.4 RPU that
dovi_tool makes after the iPhone 13's both declare exactly that (0xFFFF,
0 0 0, 12 bits, hdr_bit_depth 12), and the SDR-compatible profile 4 RPU of
dovi_tool's tests declares a gamma signal at 14 bits (39322, about 2.4 in
units of 2^-14, with three parameters), as clauses 5.4.3.3 and 5.5 compose
a base layer in BT.1886. Composed by the clause from a chart of HLG codes
(every grey code, a 21x21x21 grid of colours), the iPhone RPU's picture,
read as the PQ picture that it declares, follows the conversion of
Recommendation ITU-R BT.2100 from HLG to PQ at 1000 cd/m2 (grey code 512:
54.6 cd/m2 against 53.6; 900: 755.7 against 742.2; Delta E ITP of the
greys 6.7 on average, from the tint of its static MMR), and read as if it
were still HLG it is 83 Delta E ITP away on average: the reshaping does
the conversion, and nothing is to be converted after it.

So pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_bl_transfer takes PL_COLOR_TRC_HLG: such a
picture is composed as one whose base layer is in SMPTE ST 2084 (h at
hdr_bit_depth, no conversion) where its RPU declares its HDR picture in ST
2084 at hdr_bit_depth (pl_dovi_ccm gains signal_eotf, its parameters and
signal_bit_depth, which pl_map_dovi_metadata() fills), and libplacebo
says so once a stream; an RPU that declares another picture is not
composed, with its reason. libplacebo's own reshaping, which composes
every picture as if it were in PQ, draws the first and never the second:
the render fails, as for a base layer in BT.1886. Every other picture is
composed as before (the composing metadata gain fields, which change the
signature of its tables and not their contents).

Measured on Mesa's software OpenGL ES (zink on lavapipe), on that chart
with the two RPUs: composed with PL_COLOR_TRC_HLG, the planes are those
of a transcription of clause 5.4 in 64-bit integers, byte for byte, and
those that the composer gave before with the transfer not given; with
the RPU declaring the gamma signal, or 10 bits over a composer of 12, the
render fails and says why, by the composer and by libplacebo's reshaping
alike. The tests of libplacebo-9955 (a base layer in BT.1886) give the
same results as with it alone, and the bridge of Kodi draws every picture
of its tests to the same bytes.

Hades extension.

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, that of libplacebo and of the files changed,
whose notices stay as they are.
---
 4 files changed, 87 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/include/libplacebo/colorspace.h b/src/include/libplacebo/colorspace.h
index b7df9d7..229a725 100644
--- a/src/include/libplacebo/colorspace.h
+++ b/src/include/libplacebo/colorspace.h
@@ -196,6 +196,16 @@ struct pl_dovi_metadata {
         // mastering display, where the base layer is in BT.1886
         // (`pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_bl_transfer`)
         uint16_t source_min_pq, source_max_pq;
+        // Hades: the HDR picture that the display management metadata of
+        // the RPU describes: signal_eotf and its three parameters, and
+        // signal_bit_depth. CCM 001 sends a picture in SMPTE ST 2084 with
+        // 0xFFFF and three parameters 0 in their place (table 3), and the
+        // output of its composer with signal_bit_depth = hdr_bit_depth
+        // (clause 6.2.2). A base layer in HLG is composed where the RPU
+        // declares its picture so (`pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_bl_transfer`).
+        uint16_t signal_eotf, signal_eotf_param0, signal_eotf_param1;
+        uint32_t signal_eotf_param2;
+        uint8_t signal_bit_depth;
     } ccm;
 };
 
diff --git a/src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h b/src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h
index ffcb6cb..7f5f33d 100644
--- a/src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h
+++ b/src/include/libplacebo/renderer.h
@@ -488,12 +488,21 @@ struct pl_render_params {
     //    composed planes (also `dovi_ccm_planes`) hold that conversion. The
     //    conversion takes and gives YCbCr of BT.2020 in the narrow range, as
     //    the annex does: an RPU whose YCCtoRGB is another is not composed;
+    //  - PL_COLOR_TRC_HLG (Hades: a base layer in HLG, compatibility 4,
+    //    profile 8.4), which clause 5.2.2 a) does not name: composed as a base
+    //    layer in SMPTE ST 2084, h at hdr_bit_depth and no conversion, where
+    //    the RPU declares its HDR picture in ST 2084 at hdr_bit_depth as CCM
+    //    001 sends one (`pl_dovi_metadata.ccm.signal_eotf` 0xFFFF and its
+    //    three parameters 0, `signal_bit_depth` = hdr_bit_depth): the
+    //    reshaping of the RPU then takes the HLG signal to that picture itself.
+    //    An RPU that declares another picture is not composed;
     //  - any other transfer is not composed (clause 5.2.2 a)).
     // libplacebo's own reshaping composes every image as if its base layer
-    // were in SMPTE ST 2084. A Dolby Vision image whose base layer is in
-    // another transfer is therefore never drawn by it: where the composer of
-    // CCM 001 does not compose such an image (`dovi_ccm` off, or a reason it
-    // logs), the render fails. Hades extension.
+    // were in SMPTE ST 2084. A Dolby Vision image whose composed picture is not
+    // in ST 2084 (a base layer in BT.1886, or in HLG whose RPU does not declare
+    // ST 2084) is therefore never drawn by it: where the composer of CCM 001
+    // does not compose such an image (`dovi_ccm` off, or a reason it logs),
+    // the render fails. Hades extension.
     enum pl_color_transfer dovi_ccm_bl_transfer;
 
     // This callback is invoked for every pass successfully executed in the
diff --git a/src/include/libplacebo/utils/libav_internal.h b/src/include/libplacebo/utils/libav_internal.h
index 4dac542..2c6db64 100644
--- a/src/include/libplacebo/utils/libav_internal.h
+++ b/src/include/libplacebo/utils/libav_internal.h
@@ -1067,6 +1067,11 @@ PL_LIBAV_API void pl_map_dovi_metadata(struct pl_dovi_metadata *out,
     }
     out->ccm.source_min_pq = color->source_min_pq;
     out->ccm.source_max_pq = color->source_max_pq;
+    out->ccm.signal_eotf = color->signal_eotf;
+    out->ccm.signal_eotf_param0 = color->signal_eotf_param0;
+    out->ccm.signal_eotf_param1 = color->signal_eotf_param1;
+    out->ccm.signal_eotf_param2 = color->signal_eotf_param2;
+    out->ccm.signal_bit_depth = color->signal_bit_depth;
 }
 
 PL_DEPRECATED_IN(v7.370)
diff --git a/src/renderer.c b/src/renderer.c
index bbd283c..914a6b6 100644
--- a/src/renderer.c
+++ b/src/renderer.c
@@ -2593,12 +2593,32 @@ static pl_tex ccm_1886_down_v(struct pass_state *pass, const struct ccm_ctx *x,
     return ccm_end(pass, sh, x->fmt2, w, h, dst);
 }
 
-// Hades: the base layer of the image is not in SMPTE ST 2084
-// (pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_bl_transfer)
-static bool ccm_bl_not_pq(const struct pl_render_params *params)
+// Hades: the RPU declares its HDR picture in SMPTE ST 2084 at hdr_bit_depth,
+// as CCM 001 sends one: signal_eotf 0xFFFF with its three parameters 0 (table 3)
+// and signal_bit_depth = hdr_bit_depth (clause 6.2.2)
+static bool ccm_declares_pq(const struct pl_dovi_metadata *dovi)
 {
-    return params->dovi_ccm_bl_transfer != PL_COLOR_TRC_UNKNOWN &&
-           params->dovi_ccm_bl_transfer != PL_COLOR_TRC_PQ;
+    const struct pl_dovi_ccm *ccm = &dovi->ccm;
+    return ccm->signal_eotf == 0xFFFF && !ccm->signal_eotf_param0 &&
+           !ccm->signal_eotf_param1 && !ccm->signal_eotf_param2 &&
+           ccm->signal_bit_depth == ccm->hdr_bit_depth;
+}
+
+// Hades: the composed picture of the image would not be in SMPTE ST 2084: its
+// base layer is not, and is not one in HLG whose RPU declares its picture in
+// ST 2084 (pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_bl_transfer)
+static bool ccm_bl_not_pq(const struct pl_render_params *params,
+                          const struct pl_dovi_metadata *dovi)
+{
+    switch (params->dovi_ccm_bl_transfer) {
+    case PL_COLOR_TRC_UNKNOWN:
+    case PL_COLOR_TRC_PQ:
+        return false;
+    case PL_COLOR_TRC_HLG:
+        return !dovi || !ccm_declares_pq(dovi);
+    default:
+        return true;
+    }
 }
 
 // The EOTF of SMPTE ST 2084 for a 12-bit code, in cd/m2
@@ -2815,6 +2835,19 @@ static const char *ccm_check(struct pass_state *pass, struct ccm_ctx *x)
         break;
     case PL_COLOR_TRC_BT_1886:
         return ccm_check_bt1886(pass, x);
+    case PL_COLOR_TRC_HLG:
+        // Hades: a base layer in HLG (profile 8.4), which clause 5.2.2 a) does
+        // not name. Its RPU's reshaping takes the HLG signal to the HDR
+        // picture that the RPU's display management metadata describe; where
+        // that is one in SMPTE ST 2084 at hdr_bit_depth, as CCM 001 sends one,
+        // the samples are composed as for a base layer in ST 2084 (5.4.3.3:
+        // out_bit_depth = hdr_bit_depth; 5.5: no conversion).
+        if (!ccm_declares_pq(dovi))
+            return "a base layer in HLG whose RPU does not declare its HDR picture in SMPTE "
+                   "ST 2084 at hdr_bit_depth (signal_eotf 0xFFFF, its parameters 0, "
+                   "signal_bit_depth = hdr_bit_depth): nothing says how such a picture is "
+                   "composed";
+        break;
     default:
         return "a base layer whose transfer is neither SMPTE ST 2084 nor Recommendation "
                "ITU-R BT.1886 (clause 5.2.2 a))";
@@ -2825,15 +2858,20 @@ static const char *ccm_check(struct pass_state *pass, struct ccm_ctx *x)
 
 // Logs each reason not to compose (static strings) once a stream, and composing
 // once a stream, however often the pictures of the stream change between them.
-// (Hades: `not_pq`, a base layer that is not in SMPTE ST 2084, which nothing else
-// composes: pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_bl_transfer)
+// (Hades: `not_pq`, a composed picture that would not be in SMPTE ST 2084, which
+// nothing else composes; `transfer`, that of the base layer:
+// pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_bl_transfer)
 static void ccm_say(pl_renderer rr, struct dovi_ccm_state *st, const char *why,
-                    bool not_pq)
+                    bool not_pq, enum pl_color_transfer transfer)
 {
     if (!why) {
-        if (!st->said_composed && not_pq) {
+        if (!st->said_composed && transfer == PL_COLOR_TRC_BT_1886) {
             PL_INFO(rr, "Dolby Vision: composed as ETSI GS CCM 001 clauses 5.4 and 5.5 do "
                     "(a base layer in BT.1886, converted to SMPTE ST 2084)");
+        } else if (!st->said_composed && transfer == PL_COLOR_TRC_HLG) {
+            PL_INFO(rr, "Dolby Vision: composed as ETSI GS CCM 001 clause 5.4 does for a "
+                    "base layer in SMPTE ST 2084 (a base layer in HLG, whose RPU declares "
+                    "its HDR picture in ST 2084: its reshaping takes the HLG signal there)");
         } else if (!st->said_composed) {
             PL_INFO(rr, "Dolby Vision: composed as ETSI GS CCM 001 clause 5.4 does");
         }
@@ -2846,9 +2884,10 @@ static void ccm_say(pl_renderer rr, struct dovi_ccm_state *st, const char *why,
             return;
     }
     if (not_pq) {
-        PL_WARN(rr, "Dolby Vision: a picture whose base layer is not in SMPTE ST 2084 is "
-                "not composed as ETSI GS CCM 001 does (%s); it is not drawn (the reshaping "
-                "of libplacebo would compose it as if it were)", why);
+        PL_WARN(rr, "Dolby Vision: a picture whose base layer is not in SMPTE ST 2084 (nor "
+                "one in HLG whose RPU declares its picture in ST 2084) is not composed as "
+                "ETSI GS CCM 001 does (%s); it is not drawn (the reshaping of libplacebo "
+                "would compose it as if it were)", why);
     } else {
         PL_WARN(rr, "Dolby Vision: a picture is not composed as ETSI GS CCM 001 does "
                 "(%s); it is composed by the reshaping of libplacebo", why);
@@ -2879,7 +2918,8 @@ static bool pass_dovi_ccm(struct pass_state *pass)
         why = st->prep.reason;
     if (!why)
         why = ccm_check(pass, &x);
-    ccm_say(rr, st, why, ccm_bl_not_pq(pass->params));
+    ccm_say(rr, st, why, ccm_bl_not_pq(pass->params, dovi),
+            pass->params->dovi_ccm_bl_transfer);
     if (why)
         return false;
 
@@ -3000,19 +3040,20 @@ static bool pass_read_image(struct pass_state *pass)
     dovi_composed = pass_dovi_ccm(pass);
     if (dovi_composed)
         pass->plane_upscaler = params->dovi_ccm_plane_upscaler;
-    // Hades: a Dolby Vision image whose base layer is not in SMPTE ST 2084 is
-    // composed by the composer of CCM 001 (clause 5.5) or not at all: the
-    // reshaping of libplacebo would compose it as if it were (see
+    // Hades: a Dolby Vision image whose composed picture would not be in SMPTE
+    // ST 2084 (its base layer is not, and is not one in HLG whose RPU declares
+    // ST 2084) is composed by the composer of CCM 001 (clause 5.5) or not at
+    // all: the reshaping of libplacebo would compose it as if it were (see
     // pl_render_params.dovi_ccm_bl_transfer). The composer logged why it did
     // not; with it off, that is said here, once a stream.
     if (!dovi_composed && image->repr.sys == PL_COLOR_SYSTEM_DOLBYVISION &&
-        image->repr.dovi && ccm_bl_not_pq(params))
+        image->repr.dovi && ccm_bl_not_pq(params, image->repr.dovi))
     {
         if (!params->dovi_ccm) {
             if (!rr->dovi_ccm)
                 rr->dovi_ccm = pl_zalloc_ptr(rr, rr->dovi_ccm);
             ccm_say(rr, rr->dovi_ccm, "the composer of CCM 001 is off "
-                    "(pl_render_params.dovi_ccm)", true);
+                    "(pl_render_params.dovi_ccm)", true, params->dovi_ccm_bl_transfer);
         }
         return false;
     }
